From: MYIR Tech <support@myirtech.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 18:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm: probe: select 1080p fallback on i.MX8MP HDMI

Some HDMI sinks assert HPD but do not return EDID over DDC. The DRM probe
helper then supplies its generic fallback list, which is intentionally capped
at 1024x768. Weston consequently selects XGA on an otherwise 1080p-capable
i.MX8MP HDMI pipeline.

At the existing no-mode fallback point, use standard DMT modes through
1920x1080 and prefer 1920x1080 for an HDMI-A connector on i.MX8MP. Valid EDID
data, disconnected outputs, other connector types and other SoCs retain their
existing behaviour.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [i.MX8MP product fallback policy]
Signed-off-by: MYIR Tech <support@myirtech.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_probe_helper.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_probe_helper.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_probe_helper.c
index 5fb0b8d1f9a7..14d759acb1dc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_probe_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_probe_helper.c
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/export.h>
 #include <linux/moduleparam.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 
 #include <drm/drm_bridge.h>
 #include <drm/drm_client.h>
@@ -648,7 +649,13 @@ int drm_helper_probe_single_connector_modes(struct drm_connector *connector,
 
 	if (count == 0 && (connector->status == connector_status_connected ||
 			   connector->status == connector_status_unknown)) {
-		count = drm_add_modes_noedid(connector, 1024, 768);
+		if (connector->connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA &&
+		    of_machine_is_compatible("fsl,imx8mp")) {
+			count = drm_add_modes_noedid(connector, 1920, 1080);
+			drm_set_preferred_mode(connector, 1920, 1080);
+		} else {
+			count = drm_add_modes_noedid(connector, 1024, 768);
+		}
 
 		/*
 		 * Section 4.2.2.6 (EDID Corruption Detection) of the DP 1.4a
-- 
2.43.0
